        {
          "id": 2765366829,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "If a check like this were added to tools/check_typed_item_call.py, it could check the item's 'label' against the start of the format string.  Quite a few of these usages might just be units that would be better done with unit_strings.  Could maybe even check to see if the format string ends in one of the unit_name_string entries from unit_strings.c? \n\nI don't think I've personally used either of these APIs - if I need formatted strings I tend to use proto_item_append_text() after I've read fields beyond this one, i.e. keeping the original label and value presentation so I won't find the display filter for that field surprising.\n\nFor me, it might be more useful if there was a version of this function that already displays the label + \": \" + <value-presentation>, and any extra format+args I gave was like calling proto_item_append_text().",
          "author": {
            "id": 6810036,
            "username": "martin.r.mathieson",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Martin Mathieson",
